Imports:
  - Types:
      - AbstractHttpAdapter
    From: packages/core/adapters
  - Types:
      - HttpException
    From: packages/common/exceptions

Annotations: |
  Concrete `AbstractHttpAdapter` implementation over the Fastify HTTP library, used by
  the Fastify platform package as a higher-throughput alternative to Express.

---

"AbstractHttpAdapter::FastifyAdapter(instanceOrOptions: any)":
  location: fastify-adapter.ts
  annotations: |
    Wraps a Fastify instance (or Fastify server options used to create one) behind
    the `AbstractHttpAdapter` contract from Imports.

    `instanceOrOptions`: an existing Fastify instance, or options used to create one

    Algorithm:
    1. If the argument already looks like a Fastify instance, use it as-is; otherwise
       create a new Fastify instance from the given options, wiring a version
       constraint into its router options
    2. Register onRequest/onResponse hooks that delegate to configured
       request/response hook callbacks
  methods:
    "reply(response: any, body: any, statusCode: number)": |
      Send `body` as the Fastify reply, mirroring the Express adapter's content-type
      and streamable-file handling for the Fastify reply object.
    "mapException(error: any) -> mapped: any": |
      Convert a Fastify-internal error (one carrying an HTTP status code and
      originating from Fastify's own error type) into an `HttpException` from
      Imports constructed with that same message and status; every other error
      passes through unchanged.
    "use(args: Array<any>) -> result: any": |
      Register middleware through the Fastify middie plugin; middleware registered
      before middie has finished loading is queued and flushed once it is ready.
    "createMiddlewareFactory(requestMethod: string) -> factory: Promise<Object<string, any>>": |
      Ensure the middie plugin is registered, then build a path/callback
      registration function whose path is normalized for Fastify's router.
    "registerParserMiddleware(prefix: string, rawBody: boolean)": |
      Register Fastify content-type parsers for JSON and URL-encoded bodies exactly
      once, deferring to Fastify's own default JSON parser under the hood.
    "initHttpServer()": |
      Bind the adapter's underlying HTTP server property to the Fastify instance's
      own underlying native server.
    "close() -> done: Promise<void>": |
      Abstract override. Close the Fastify instance, releasing the underlying
      server.

---

Author: Goga
CreatedAt: 26/08/26
Description: |
  Documents the Fastify platform adapter as a second concrete mutation of
  `AbstractHttpAdapter`, alongside the Express adapter, to make the platform-adapter
  boundary's polymorphism explicit: both adapters satisfy one shared contract while
  differing entirely in how they register middleware and shape responses.
